  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political landscape in Indonesia is currently focused on the selection of a new vice president to replace Gibran. Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, serving as the daily chairman of the Gerindra Party and Deputy Speaker of the DPR RI, has emerged as a significant name in discussions regarding potential successors. Various stakeholders, including political parties like PAN and other organizations, have expressed support for candidates aligned with the ideological direction of President Prabowo Subianto. Observers emphasize that the incoming official must be capable of addressing regional aspirations. According to constitutional requirements, the president is obligated to submit two names for the position 14 days prior to the relevant parliamentary plenary session. While speculation continues regarding the candidate pool, Dasco has publicly maintained that the final decision rests solely on the presidential prerogative and has committed to respecting the ongoing selection process.",
